The control for peers-algos (PARALLEL.md, C): the data part of its plan
alone, on a copy of the whole project with a mem of its own. The three
controls run at once show how fast three sessions do the three groups on
this box with no plan shared.

-- mem --
c := mem.Todo("data: lru, intervals and topo").Parallel()
c.Todo("write the LRU Cache in lru/lru.go (its check: go test ./lru/)")
c.Todo("write Merge in intervals/intervals.go (its check: go test ./intervals/)")
c.Todo("write Sort in topo/topo.go (its check: go test ./topo/)")
-- prompt-new --
Work through the plan in mem until nothing is left for you.
-- check --
cmd go test ./lru/ ./intervals/ ./topo/
cmd echo '0c17f32e3795f05fcd6c8cc73249a0c3b841d8d134f4ad0376a9dca0f301d77b  lru/lru_test.go' | sha256sum -c --quiet
cmd echo '392b1dce39eb25633a375403191a59a283b142be4f390723b5fe64aa42ba9784  intervals/intervals_test.go' | sha256sum -c --quiet
cmd echo '00d3ace9ee2b45dd6f976a429524a22b395dc8df63325f2310bfeae9cde30b66  topo/topo_test.go' | sha256sum -c --quiet
mem-count done >= 4
mem-count open == 0
